# Railway And Deployment

- Follow `AGENTS.md` before changing deployment surfaces.
- Do not rename, delete, merge, or repurpose Railway services automatically.
- Do not change production Railway variables, domains, database URLs, or service identities automatically.
- Do not point staging services at production Supabase.
- Root `railway.json` is the web app. `worker/railway.json`, `worker/railway.noc-proof-erecord.json`, and `worker/railway.ops.json` are separate workers. `marketing/railway.json` is separate marketing deployment.
- A root `npm run build` does not validate worker containers. Worker changes need service-specific syntax/build checks when safe.
- Trigger.dev is control-plane orchestration only; Playwright stays on Railway workers.
- Env var additions must update `.env.staging.example` and `.env.production.example` with placeholders only.
- Never run `npm run trigger:deploy` or production deploy/replay commands as validation.
